      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The WTO, in its current form, is facing severe structural challenges because it was designed for a different, more cooperative era. The current reality of great power competition makes the consensus-driven nature of the WTO too slow and ineffective to handle modern geopolitical risks. Instead of a complete end, we are seeing a fragmentation where regional blocs and bilateral deals are replacing the broad, universal agreements of the past. This new system favors national security and industrial resilience over pure market efficiency.",
      "source": "target",
