      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The argument that prioritizing national security leads to inefficiency is a fundamental economic critique of the status quo, but it ignores the strategic risks of over-reliance on adversaries. When critical supply chains are controlled by geopolitical rivals, the risk of economic coercion or disruption far outweighs the cost of slightly higher domestic production. Therefore, resilience is not just a preference; it is a necessary defense against economic warfare. A truly secure economy is one that can function even when global trade relations sour.",
